{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "**Observations**\n- In pod logs for `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf`, repeated warnings show `db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)` alongside growing heap pressure at 360 MB / 512 MB.\n- In deployment `billing-api` spec, `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` is configured to `900` seconds.\n- In deployment record `CI-2455`, load balancer idle timeout was set to 120 seconds while application HTTP keep-alive was raised to 125 seconds.\n\n**Root cause**\nDatabase connection pool idle recycling delay (900 seconds) exceeds the upstream network idle timeout, causing connection pool exhaustion from dead sockets per runbook `RB-014` and post-mortem `INC-2024-0312`.\n\n**Recommended action**\nThe billing development team should lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` in deployment `billing-api` below upstream network idle timeout thresholds.\n\n**Ruled-out leads**\n- Application memory leak ruled out because memory growth is a byproduct of stalled database connections holding memory, as documented in runbook `RB-007` and post-mortem `INC-2024-0312`.\n- EBS degraded performance in `eu-west-3a` from bulletin `AWS-2026-0903-01` ruled out because failures stem from connection resets rather than EBS storage latency.",
